ot/issues/comments/2689198339/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2689632372","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103243#issuecomment-2689632372","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103243","id":2689632372,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gUIh0","user":{"login":"matt08-prog","id":58103083,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4MTAzMDgz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58103083?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matt08-prog","html_url":"https://github.com/matt08-prog","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matt08-prog/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matt08-prog/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matt08-prog/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matt08-prog/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matt08-prog/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matt08-prog/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matt08-prog/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matt08-prog/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matt08-prog/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-28T03:27:49Z","updated_at":"2025-02-28T03:27:49Z","body":"> The way argument options are implemented requires an instance of the type at the moment. Based on typing and control flow there might not always be a reduced value for a variable (in particular when casting with `as`), in those cases argument option completion won't work, so this isn't an issue limited to group methods. [#85364](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/85364) should fix this (for instantiatable types), if you can build it yourself you migh